{
 "_why": "Verification record for the 32 released Defense Intelligence Reference Documents, produced by downloading every PDF and reading it. It is kept in the repo because the verification is expensive to redo and the downloads themselves are ephemeral: 78MB of PDFs that lived in a container temp directory. Anything asserted on a DIRD edge or claim should be checkable against this file without fetching anything.\n\nTwo passes were needed and the first was wrong. Reading only the first three pages found 13 of 32 naming the Advanced Aerospace Weapon System Applications Program; scanning the whole document found 27. The five that do not name it anywhere are recorded as such, and their aawsap edges are Tier 2 resting on the DIA 9 January 2018 list rather than on the document.\n\nThe scans are heavily OCR-degraded - the inside-cover statement images as 'advanced technalo re arts roduced' - so a document number was only recorded where it read unambiguously as DIA-NN-NNNN-NNN. 12 of 32 did. Publication dates read cleanly on all 32.",
 "_read_on": "2026-08-22 (covers) and 2026-08-23 (full-document scan)",
